WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.124 --> 00:00:02.213
(audience cheering)

00:00:02.213 --> 00:00:03.116
- [Kelly] Good to see you.

00:00:03.116 --> 00:00:04.207
- [Kyra] Thank you.

00:00:04.207 --> 00:00:08.842
(audience continues cheering)

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.754
- I know. I know.

00:00:10.754 --> 00:00:12.270
I've been very excited.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.400
I'm now meeting the whole
family except Travis,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.710
but I've met Sosie now, I've met him

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.278
and I'm very excited to meet you.

00:00:18.278 --> 00:00:19.619
- Thank you.
- I'm like a big fan.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.452
- Thank you.
- Do you guys get into

00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:22.733
March Madness? We were
talking about it earlier.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.320
- Since I didn't go to college

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I don't have much skin in the
game for any particular team

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.150
but I do like to catch up to it

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.190
and that's when I start watching

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.450
and I fill out a bracket

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.320
and, you know...
- Yeah.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.760
- I was trying to explain

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.907
in the dressing room, Kyra was like

00:00:36.907 --> 00:00:38.790
"What's a bracket?".
- A bracket? What's a bracket?

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.230
- Oh you're me. So now I know,

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.120
but my friends are really into sports ball

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.200
so I had to do it.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.590
And then I usually pick like
favorite colors or mascots

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.390
and then I just go with it. (laughing)

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:52.590
I get a part. It's like they
eliminate each other each time.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.480
I know a little bit more now.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.700
Well wait, this is gonna
be, is it 35 years?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.660
- [Kyra] Yes.
- So you're about to celebrate

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.581
35 years together?
- Yes

00:00:58.581 --> 00:01:01.963
(audience cheering)
- That's incredible.

00:01:01.963 --> 00:01:02.796
- Well...

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:03.629
- That's incredible.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:05.280
I'm just saying it doesn't always happen,

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.600
especially for people in the business,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.800
especially for two artists.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.360
Like, that's incredible.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.010
Let me know like what your secret is.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.534
Maybe I'll use it next time, like yeah.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.367
- We have no secret

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:15.510
- We have no secrets, yes.
- Are y'all doing

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.490
anything big? Are you doing
anything to celebrate?

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.760
- We don't usually do a big
thing for our anniversary.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:24.629
We usually like hang out
and go to dinner, you know.

00:01:24.629 --> 00:01:25.462
I mean, really we're--
- Yeah.

00:01:25.462 --> 00:01:26.295
- [Kevin] We make dinner.

00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:27.128
- Yeah.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:27.961
- Yeah.

00:01:27.961 --> 00:01:29.040
- We're pretty boring.
- But that's nice.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.990
But I feel like our jobs
are always constantly going

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.160
and doing stuff, so it's nice to do--

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.039
- [Kyra] Yes exactly.

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:33.872
Exactly, exactly.
- Yeah.

00:01:33.872 --> 00:01:35.070
- I think one of the things we like

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.140
about our anniversary
though, I have to say,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.610
is that it falls in September

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.319
and I absolutely love the
month of September because it--

00:01:40.319 --> 00:01:41.280
- [Kelly] Ooh, fall in general.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.140
- Yeah. I mean, the light is so beautiful.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.530
And also, for some reason New Years

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:49.200
is supposed to be the start of the year

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.060
but it never feels like the
start of the year for me.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:54.090
September feels like when the year starts.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:54.930
It's hopeful.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.669
- [Kelly] Yeah.
(audience coos)

00:01:56.669 --> 00:01:57.502
And you think that
coincides with like school--

00:01:57.502 --> 00:01:58.886
- Is that corny I don't know I--

00:01:58.886 --> 00:02:00.420
- No, do you think that--
- I wasn't even trying

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.591
to elicit an aw but somehow
just talking about September

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.033
got an aw.
- For my family

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.800
it's because I have kids.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.573
So it's like school starts around then.

00:02:09.573 --> 00:02:10.406
- [Kyra] Yes. Yes, exactly.

00:02:10.406 --> 00:02:11.239
- Yeah, right.
- So it feels like the school

00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:12.072
year kind of starts for me too.

00:02:12.072 --> 00:02:14.028
In a totally non-romantic way.
- Exactly.

00:02:14.028 --> 00:02:15.746
- Just that's when I buy school supplies.

00:02:15.746 --> 00:02:17.390
So, that's what it is.
- Yes exactly.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.590
- So when Kevin was here he had a story

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.570
about you hating your engagement ring.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.403
- [Kyra] Oh God.

00:02:22.403 --> 00:02:23.236
- Which I love.

00:02:23.236 --> 00:02:24.990
- Ugh.
- So is this true?

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:25.950
- You loved her engagement ring?

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.470
- No. I love the story of her being--

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.660
You knew y'all were gonna
make it when she could be

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.880
that level of honest.
- That's right. That's right.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.380
It took me like two weeks

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.880
to be that level of honest.
- Two weeks?

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.980
It would've taken me years.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.510
- (laughing) Right?
- Yeah. That's honesty though.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:40.427
Like, that's amazing that you, yeah.

00:02:40.427 --> 00:02:42.690
- It was pretty intense.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.310
It's one of those things where you like--

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.610
I knew that you had spent a
lot of time looking for it,

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:48.630
just the right one.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.360
And, you know, I looked at it
and every time I looked at it,

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.687
I was like, "This isn't
me. This isn't right."

00:02:52.687 --> 00:02:55.560
- Yeah.
- And so we...

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.110
I had to, you know, one
night we went to sleep

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.693
and he falls asleep in about 30 seconds.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:05.520
And I sort of was rolling
around and I turned on the light

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.480
and I was like, "I gotta say it",

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.427
I turned on the light, I woke
up and he's like, "What?"

00:03:08.427 --> 00:03:10.470
And I said, "I'm so sorry.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.900
I love you so much, but I
really don't like the ring."

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.137
And he was like,
(laughing)

00:03:14.137 --> 00:03:17.370
"Oh my God! I thought it
was something serious!"

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.297
And then the next morning he was like,

00:03:19.297 --> 00:03:21.840
"I feel really bad that
you don't like the ring."

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.490
- Oh.
- "I worked really hard

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.920
trying to find it." And
I felt bad, but you know,

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.330
better to do it then.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.327
- No. Better to be honest.
- Just rip off the bandaid.

00:03:29.327 --> 00:03:30.630
- This is the secret.
- Rip off.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.340
- Right off the bat.
- Yes. Exactly.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.173
- I love it.
(audience coos)

00:03:33.173 --> 00:03:34.693
I love that you were like two weeks.

00:03:34.693 --> 00:03:36.090
(chuckles) It would take me two years.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:36.923
I love that.

00:03:36.923 --> 00:03:38.700
Their new film is called "Space Oddity."

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.620
Kyra directed it and Kevin stars in it.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.933
So Kyra, why did you
wanna make this movie?

00:03:44.731 --> 00:03:45.804
Because you were choosing
to direct something.

00:03:45.804 --> 00:03:46.637
- Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:46.637 --> 00:03:50.340
- On the face of it's a
really beautiful story

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.600
about a young man who
grew up on a flower farm

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.400
and decides that in his twenties
he wants out of the Earth

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.630
and he wants to go to Mars.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:04.950
So he thinks he's training
for a one way journey to Mars.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.370
And basically he lives with
his family on this flower farm

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.620
and he falls in love with
a young woman in the town

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.970
and then ends up not going.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.980
So that's like the surface of it, right?

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.210
- Yeah.
- It's funny, it's sad,

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:18.690
it's hopeful, but ultimately
it's really about grief

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:22.740
and about how when we grieve
and when we've lost someone

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.110
and when something happens
that's painful in our life,

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.960
sometimes we scatter away from each other

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.720
and away from the world and
we wanna just check out.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.820
And he's checking out in a major way

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.400
by wanting to go to Mars,
but we all check out, right?

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.630
- Yeah.
- And this is a family

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.410
that's coming to terms
with the loss of a child.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.590
And so they're all checking
out in one way or another

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.090
and they have to come back together.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.850
And it's basically about
fighting the good fight

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:48.960
here on Earth.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.530
Life is messy. Life is
sad, things are scary,

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:55.740
people die, the Earth
is struggling right now,

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:57.660
but we have to try and
make a go of it here.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.280
There isn't a planet B.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.240
There's no planet B.
- Yeah.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.830
There's no like...

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:02.860
You know, we need each other.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.250
- Yeah.
- And so, that's ultimately--

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.400
it had so many great
messages and such great fun

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.290
and romance and like...

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.550
- Yeah.
- So many great things

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.100
about it that I was
like, "This is the one."

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.660
- What a great teaser.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.323
That was incredible.
- Thank you.

00:05:17.323 --> 00:05:18.930
- Yeah. Well, I wanna talk about your son,

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.400
'cause I think I think this is so cool.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.810
So Travis does music.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:22.740
- Yes.
- And how did he

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:23.880
get involved with the film?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.740
- Yeah, Travis is a great musician,

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:27.480
has been from the time he was...

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:28.950
I mean, he had the
first guitar in his hand

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.950
when he was like eight or
something, or maybe even younger.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:35.700
And he did the music for my first movie

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.250
for my first movie
called "Story of a Girl."

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.590
He said, you know, "I have some ideas."

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:41.497
He read the script, he was like

00:05:41.497 --> 00:05:46.497
"I've got some ideas for theme and score.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.600
I mean, I'll just give it a
shot and see what you think."

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.340
And I'm like, "Okay."

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.034
'Cause I just didn't know.
- Yeah.

00:05:52.034 --> 00:05:53.340
- You thought you were
gonna have to turn him down.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.690
- Yeah, I did, I did.
- Yeah.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.160
- And then it was incredible.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:56.993
- Oh wow!

00:05:56.993 --> 00:05:57.990
- And then he did "Space Oddity"

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.850
which is a whole nother vibe.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:01.260
- Yeah.
- And no, he's incredible,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.580
he's a really great composer.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.960
- It's a beautiful thing though,

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.530
you don't think about how many
people go into each episode

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:08.700
of a show or a movie.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.680
You don't think about
all those people that are

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.470
in the background making
this one scene happen.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.150
- Yeah. Oh yeah.
- It's a really magical thing

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:16.200
that y'all get to be a part of.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.550
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.200
Anyway, I was just gonna say that.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.990
Well, sometimes the family
plays music with goats.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:23.430
So, quick question.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:24.334
Why?

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:25.350
(laughter)

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.460
- [Kyra] Good question.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.810
- [Kelly] Like what? (chuckles)

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:29.520
- [Kevin] The goats showed
up, we've had a farm

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.816
for a long time.
- (laughing) This is awesome.

00:06:31.816 --> 00:06:34.620
- (chuckling) Playing
a little ukulele there.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:35.790
- I had pygmies once.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:36.810
Like they're, I love goats.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:37.643
- [Kevin] Yeah goats are awe--

00:06:37.643 --> 00:06:38.610
- They will eat everything though, yes.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:39.720
- Yeah, no they're great.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:40.830
That's...

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.090
- They will eat your clothes.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:43.690
- That was Hocus and Little Man.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.503
Yeah.

00:06:45.503 --> 00:06:48.570
We had a farm for a really long time

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.510
and always had big horses.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.990
But on our anniversary,

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:56.760
actually I think it was
during the pandemic.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:57.593
- [Kyra] Yeah.

00:06:57.593 --> 00:07:02.420
- I snuck out and went and got
a couple of miniature goats,

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.170
pygmies, and stuck them
in one of the stalls

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.120
and then said "Happy Anniversary".

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.900
And took her down and
introduced her to these goats.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:17.900
And one day I was just
fooling around and went down

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:23.400
and took an instrument down
there and just started playing.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.532
And I don't know,

00:07:24.532 --> 00:07:27.930
(chuckling) they seemed like
they liked it. (laughing)

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:30.000
- You're like, "I'm a
hit here." (laughing)

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.230
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.693
- Right. Nobody else
is gonna listen to me.

00:07:32.693 --> 00:07:33.900
(laughing)

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:34.890
So I'll let the goats.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.300
- I totally sing to my animals.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.849
I was being funny when I said
"why" but I totally do it too.

00:07:38.849 --> 00:07:40.227
- Yeah. I mean they're very soothing.

00:07:40.227 --> 00:07:42.210
- Not like too them almost,
just like, kind of with them,

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.970
and then they sit there
while you're loving on them.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.140
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.550
- It's very soothing.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:48.383
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:48.383 --> 00:07:51.480
- I mean, it's soothing
for us to be with them.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.590
- Exactly.
- And then,

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:53.880
you know, music has the same thing.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:58.080
So then I just took it
and started picking songs

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.360
that I thought, and started
this series called "Goat Songs."

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.280
And sometimes Kyra's been there with me

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:04.770
and sometimes Sosie and yeah,
we've done a lot of them.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:07.076
- Yeah.
- I love your family so much.

00:08:07.076 --> 00:08:08.760
(chuckling) It's so random.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:09.870
I love it so much.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:11.460
Well, later we actually have music

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:14.010
from one of the organizations
that you guys worked with.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.870
We're super excited about it.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.227
But we need to take a quick break.

00:08:17.227 --> 00:08:19.350
"Space Oddity" is in
theaters starting today

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.033
and on demand so go see it.

